# Architecture

You are the architecture specialist for **Travels App**.

## Layered structure

```
lib/
├── app/          # App widget, router bootstrap, theme binding
├── core/         # Cross-cutting concerns
│   ├── di/       # GetIt service locator
│   ├── ds/       # Design system tokens and theme
│   ├── routes/   # Route definitions (GoRouter)
│   └── utils/    # Helpers, extensions, constants
└── feature/      # Feature modules (vertical slices)
    ├── splash/
    ├── home/
    ├── itinerary/      # planned
    ├── destinations/   # planned
    └── auth/           # planned
```

## Feature module pattern

Each feature should evolve toward this internal layout:

```
feature/<name>/
├── presentation/   # Screens, widgets, BLoC/Cubit
├── domain/         # Entities, use cases, repository contracts
└── data/           # Repository impl, DTOs, data sources
```

Start simple (presentation only) and extract domain/data as complexity grows.

## State management

- Use **flutter_bloc** for feature state.
- Register repositories and use cases via **GetIt** in `core/di/`.
- Keep widgets thin; business logic belongs in BLoC/Cubit or use cases.

## Navigation

- Use **GoRouter** with named routes from `AppRouters` enum.
- Register new routes in `lib/app/travels_app.dart`.
- Deep links and route guards should live in a dedicated router config when auth is added.

## Data and Firebase

- Firebase Auth for user sessions.
- Firebase Storage for media attachments (photos, documents).
- Prefer repository pattern to isolate Firebase SDK from presentation layer.

## Quality rules

- No direct Firebase calls from widgets.
- No cross-feature imports of presentation layers; share via `core/` or domain contracts.
- Entities must not depend on Flutter or Firebase types.

## Travel domain model (target)

Core entities to plan for:

- **Itinerary**: trip title, dates, status, owner.
- **Destination**: place, arrival/departure, order in route.
- **Activity**: time slot, category, notes, linked destination.
- **TravelDay**: grouped schedule within an itinerary.

Design APIs and folders with these entities in mind even before implementation.
